project Sieve
target console
runtime AgentRuntime 0.1

entry console main

error MainError
errorCase MainError AllocationFailed Int32
errorCase MainError ConsoleWriteFailed Int32

operation main
input operation main console Console
output operation main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main read clock.cpu
effect main write console.stdout
effect main allocate heap
effect main free heap
effect main write memory.buffer
effect main read memory.buffer
memory main heap yes
memory main stack max 8KiB
async main no

purpose operation main "Run the Sieve of Eratosthenes up to sieveUpperLimit repeatedly and report the summed prime count plus elapsed seconds"
invariant operation main "A sieve cell holds one while its index is still prime and zero once struck out as composite"
invariant operation main "Composite marking only needs candidates up to the square root of sieveUpperLimit, since every composite has a prime factor at or below its square root"
invariant operation main "Elapsed seconds equals elapsed CPU-clock ticks divided by the Windows CLOCKS_PER_SEC of 1000"

label startMain

storage module immutable sieveUpperLimit Int64 2000000
storage module immutable sieveByteArraySize ByteCount 2000001
storage module immutable sieveRepeatCount Int64 40
storage module immutable firstCandidateIndex Int64 2
storage module immutable firstCountIndex Int64 2
storage module immutable loopStepIncrement Int64 1
storage module immutable primeCellMarker Int32 1
storage module immutable compositeCellMarker Int32 0
storage module immutable primeCellFillByte Int64 1
storage module immutable zeroIndex Int64 0
storage module immutable oneIndex Int64 1
storage module immutable repeatIndexInitial Int64 0
storage module immutable primeCountInitial Int64 0
storage module immutable windowsClocksPerSecond Float64 1000.0

call sieveAllocateCall c.malloc
argument sieveAllocateCall size ByteCount sieveByteArraySize
run sieveAllocateCall
bind value sieveBuffer OpaquePointer sieveAllocateCall

memory main mutable currentRepeatIndex Int64 repeatIndexInitial
memory main mutable totalPrimeCount Int64 primeCountInitial
memory main mutable currentPrimeCount Int64 primeCountInitial
memory main mutable currentCandidateIndex Int64 firstCandidateIndex
memory main mutable currentMultipleIndex Int64 firstCandidateIndex
memory main mutable currentCountIndex Int64 firstCountIndex

call benchmarkStartClockCall c.clock
run benchmarkStartClockCall
bind value benchmarkStartClockTicks CpuClockTicks benchmarkStartClockCall

label repeatLoopHead
call repeatShouldContinueCall math.lessThanInt64
argument repeatShouldContinueCall left Int64 currentRepeatIndex
argument repeatShouldContinueCall right Int64 sieveRepeatCount
run repeatShouldContinueCall
bind value repeatShouldContinue Bool repeatShouldContinueCall
branch if condition repeatShouldContinue target repeatLoopBody
branch else target repeatLoopFinished

label repeatLoopBody
# Start every cell as prime, then strike out indices 0 and 1 which are not.
call sievePrimeFillCall c.memset
argument sievePrimeFillCall buffer OpaquePointer sieveBuffer
argument sievePrimeFillCall fillByte Int64 primeCellFillByte
argument sievePrimeFillCall byteCount ByteCount sieveByteArraySize
run sievePrimeFillCall
bind value sievePrimeFillReturn OpaquePointer sievePrimeFillCall

call strikeZeroCall pointer.storeByte
argument strikeZeroCall buffer OpaquePointer sieveBuffer
argument strikeZeroCall offset Int64 zeroIndex
argument strikeZeroCall value Int32 compositeCellMarker
run strikeZeroCall

call strikeOneCall pointer.storeByte
argument strikeOneCall buffer OpaquePointer sieveBuffer
argument strikeOneCall offset Int64 oneIndex
argument strikeOneCall value Int32 compositeCellMarker
run strikeOneCall

set memory currentCandidateIndex firstCandidateIndex
jump target candidateLoopHead

label candidateLoopHead
# Continue while currentCandidateIndex squared is still within the limit.
call candidateSquaredGuardCall math.multiplyInt64
argument candidateSquaredGuardCall left Int64 currentCandidateIndex
argument candidateSquaredGuardCall right Int64 currentCandidateIndex
run candidateSquaredGuardCall
bind value candidateSquaredGuard Int64 candidateSquaredGuardCall

call candidateShouldContinueCall math.lessThanOrEqualInt64
argument candidateShouldContinueCall left Int64 candidateSquaredGuard
argument candidateShouldContinueCall right Int64 sieveUpperLimit
run candidateShouldContinueCall
bind value candidateShouldContinue Bool candidateShouldContinueCall
branch if condition candidateShouldContinue target candidateLoopBody
branch else target candidateLoopFinished

label candidateLoopBody
call loadCandidateCellCall pointer.loadByte
argument loadCandidateCellCall buffer OpaquePointer sieveBuffer
argument loadCandidateCellCall offset Int64 currentCandidateIndex
run loadCandidateCellCall
bind value candidateCellValue Int8 loadCandidateCellCall

call candidateIsPrimeCall math.notEqualInt64
argument candidateIsPrimeCall left Int64 candidateCellValue
argument candidateIsPrimeCall right Int64 primeCountInitial
run candidateIsPrimeCall
bind value candidateIsPrime Bool candidateIsPrimeCall
branch if condition candidateIsPrime target candidateIsPrimeStep
branch else target candidateAdvance

label candidateIsPrimeStep
set memory currentMultipleIndex candidateSquaredGuard
jump target markLoopHead

label markLoopHead
call markShouldContinueCall math.lessThanOrEqualInt64
argument markShouldContinueCall left Int64 currentMultipleIndex
argument markShouldContinueCall right Int64 sieveUpperLimit
run markShouldContinueCall
bind value markShouldContinue Bool markShouldContinueCall
branch if condition markShouldContinue target markLoopBody
branch else target candidateAdvance

label markLoopBody
call markCompositeCall pointer.storeByte
argument markCompositeCall buffer OpaquePointer sieveBuffer
argument markCompositeCall offset Int64 currentMultipleIndex
argument markCompositeCall value Int32 compositeCellMarker
run markCompositeCall

call advanceMultipleCall math.addInt64
argument advanceMultipleCall left Int64 currentMultipleIndex
argument advanceMultipleCall right Int64 currentCandidateIndex
run advanceMultipleCall
bind value nextMultipleIndex Int64 advanceMultipleCall
set memory currentMultipleIndex nextMultipleIndex
jump target markLoopHead

label candidateAdvance
call advanceCandidateCall math.addInt64
argument advanceCandidateCall left Int64 currentCandidateIndex
argument advanceCandidateCall right Int64 loopStepIncrement
run advanceCandidateCall
bind value nextCandidateIndex Int64 advanceCandidateCall
set memory currentCandidateIndex nextCandidateIndex
jump target candidateLoopHead

label candidateLoopFinished
# Count surviving primes in a final pass over indices 2..sieveUpperLimit.
set memory currentPrimeCount primeCountInitial
set memory currentCountIndex firstCountIndex
jump target countLoopHead

label countLoopHead
call countShouldContinueCall math.lessThanOrEqualInt64
argument countShouldContinueCall left Int64 currentCountIndex
argument countShouldContinueCall right Int64 sieveUpperLimit
run countShouldContinueCall
bind value countShouldContinue Bool countShouldContinueCall
branch if condition countShouldContinue target countLoopBody
branch else target countLoopFinished

label countLoopBody
call loadCountCellCall pointer.loadByte
argument loadCountCellCall buffer OpaquePointer sieveBuffer
argument loadCountCellCall offset Int64 currentCountIndex
run loadCountCellCall
bind value countCellValue Int8 loadCountCellCall

call accumulatePrimeCountCall math.addInt64
argument accumulatePrimeCountCall left Int64 currentPrimeCount
argument accumulatePrimeCountCall right Int64 countCellValue
run accumulatePrimeCountCall
bind value nextPrimeCount Int64 accumulatePrimeCountCall
set memory currentPrimeCount nextPrimeCount

call advanceCountIndexCall math.addInt64
argument advanceCountIndexCall left Int64 currentCountIndex
argument advanceCountIndexCall right Int64 loopStepIncrement
run advanceCountIndexCall
bind value nextCountIndex Int64 advanceCountIndexCall
set memory currentCountIndex nextCountIndex
jump target countLoopHead

label countLoopFinished
call accumulateTotalPrimeCountCall math.addInt64
argument accumulateTotalPrimeCountCall left Int64 totalPrimeCount
argument accumulateTotalPrimeCountCall right Int64 currentPrimeCount
run accumulateTotalPrimeCountCall
bind value nextTotalPrimeCount Int64 accumulateTotalPrimeCountCall
set memory totalPrimeCount nextTotalPrimeCount

call advanceRepeatCall math.addInt64
argument advanceRepeatCall left Int64 currentRepeatIndex
argument advanceRepeatCall right Int64 loopStepIncrement
run advanceRepeatCall
bind value nextRepeatIndex Int64 advanceRepeatCall
set memory currentRepeatIndex nextRepeatIndex
jump target repeatLoopHead

label repeatLoopFinished

call benchmarkEndClockCall c.clock
run benchmarkEndClockCall
bind value benchmarkEndClockTicks CpuClockTicks benchmarkEndClockCall

call elapsedClockTicksCall math.subtractInt64
argument elapsedClockTicksCall left CpuClockTicks benchmarkEndClockTicks
argument elapsedClockTicksCall right CpuClockTicks benchmarkStartClockTicks
run elapsedClockTicksCall
bind value elapsedClockTicks Int64 elapsedClockTicksCall

call elapsedClockTicksAsFloatCall math.convertInt64ToFloat64
argument elapsedClockTicksAsFloatCall value Int64 elapsedClockTicks
run elapsedClockTicksAsFloatCall
bind value elapsedClockTicksAsFloat Float64 elapsedClockTicksAsFloatCall

call elapsedSecondsCall math.divideFloat64
argument elapsedSecondsCall left Float64 elapsedClockTicksAsFloat
argument elapsedSecondsCall right Float64 windowsClocksPerSecond
run elapsedSecondsCall
bind value elapsedSeconds Float64 elapsedSecondsCall

storage module immutable reportFormatText String "checksum=%lld elapsedSeconds=%.6f\n"
call reportCall c.printf
argument reportCall format String reportFormatText
argument reportCall checksum Int64 totalPrimeCount
argument reportCall elapsedSeconds Float64 elapsedSeconds
run reportCall
ignore void source reportCall
bind error reportError Int32 reportCall
branch error source reportCall target consoleWriteFailed

call sieveFreeCall c.free
argument sieveFreeCall pointer OpaquePointer sieveBuffer
run sieveFreeCall

storage module immutable successfulExitCode ExitCode 0
return ok successfulExitCode

label consoleWriteFailed
makeError consoleWriteFailure MainError.ConsoleWriteFailed reportError
return error consoleWriteFailure
